spec dd07-ddl-in-read-tx: 2 sessions, 4 permutations
# DD07, read-only transaction. s1 issues CREATE INDEX inside BEGIN READ, then reads
# and commits; s2 creates another index in an autocommit statement. The DDL in the
# read-only transaction is ErrWriteInReadOnlyTx (F9) and creates nothing; the read
# that follows still answers.

starting permutation: s1ddl s1r s1c s2ix
step s1ddl: CREATE INDEX l_s FOR (n:L) ON (n.s)
ERROR: cypher: write or DDL statement not allowed in a read-only transaction
step s1r: MATCH (n:L) RETURN count(n) AS c
c
-
1
(1 row)
step s1c: COMMIT
step s2ix: CREATE INDEX l_name FOR (n:L) ON (n.name)
final fschema: <schema>
kind |name            |definition
-----+----------------+----------
index|l_name          |          
index|l_name_btree_num|          
